In this exclusive interview on The Capitol Show, Maria Maalouf sits down with Christopher Nixon Cox, businessman, investor, political figure, and grandson of President Richard Nixon, for a wide-ranging conversation about American leadership and the rapidly changing global order.

Cox reflects on President Nixon’s foreign-policy legacy and explains why he believes Nixon’s historic opening to China was a strategic success that helped reshape the Cold War. He discusses how Washington should confront China today while still recognizing the need for cooperation between the world’s two major powers.

The conversation also explores the similarities between Richard Nixon’s foreign-policy realism and President Donald Trump’s “America First” approach, including their views on American power, national interests, and the role of strong U.S. allies.

On Iran, Cox argues that the rise of the Islamic Republic fundamentally destabilized the Middle East, praises President Trump for confronting the Iranian threat, and discusses what could come next for U.S. policy toward Tehran.

Looking ahead to the 2026 midterm elections, Cox offers his assessment of Republican prospects in the House and Senate and explains how the Republican Party has evolved from the John McCain era to the Trump era — particularly on immigration, foreign intervention, and populism.

The interview also turns to NATO, artificial intelligence and national security, with Cox arguing that technological leadership will be essential if the United States intends to remain the world’s leading power.

And finally, Maria asks him a personal question:

If Richard Nixon could sit down with President Trump today for one hour, what would they agree on?

His answer: “The greatness of the United States.”

